# .dockerignore
#
# Anything listed here is excluded from the **build context** sent to the
# Docker daemon for *every* Dockerfile in the repository (the root
# `Dockerfile`, the new `Dockerfile.hackathon`, and any future variants).
# Smaller context = faster builds + smaller chance of accidentally baking a
# secret into a layer.

# --- Node / TS build output --------------------------------------------------
# `node_modules` is rebuilt inside the image; sending it just bloats context.
node_modules
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# TypeScript output is reproduced by `npm run build` in the image.
dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test coverage reports are regenerated by CI and have no runtime value.
coverage
.nyc_output

# Prisma client cache is regenerated by `prisma generate` inside the image.
.prisma

# --- Source control + CI -----------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- Secrets and local environment files ------------------------------------
# Critically important: never let `.env*` files leak into the image. Operators
# always inject runtime secrets via `docker run --env-file`, `docker compose
# env_file:`, or Kubernetes/Swarm secrets.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Editor / OS noise -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea
.vscode/*.log
.history

# --- Test fixtures -----------------------------------------------------------
# Tests run in CI; nothing here is needed by the runtime image.
src/tests
src/**/*.spec.ts
src/**/*.test.ts
__tests__
jest.config.*
jest.setup.*

# --- Logs --------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs

# --- Documentation / scripts that aren't needed at runtime -------------------
# README, docs/, and top-level scripts are useful for humans but bloat the
# image. Keep `scripts/install-bindings.js` and similar build-time helpers out.
docs
scripts

# --- Top-level repo metadata not needed in the image ------------------------
LICENSE
.eslintrc*
.prettierrc*
.editorconfig
